- **Tamper evidence beyond DB grants**: SOC2/PCI-grade auditors often want more than "the app role can't UPDATE it" — consider a hash chain (each row stores `sha256(prev_hash || row content)`) so deletion-by-superuser or `TRUNCATE` is detectable, or periodic export to WORM storage (S3 Object Lock) for retention past your DB's lifecycle.
